<title>UK: Belgium sets $400 million May 1999 bond.</title>
<headline>Belgium sets $400 million May 1999 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Deutsche Morgan Grenfell.</p>
<p> BORROWER   KINGDOM OF BELGIUM</p>
<p> AMT    $400 MLN	COUPON     6.0	 MATURITY    25.MAY.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.995   PAY DATE   S20.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.125     REOFFER    99.995    SPREAD	+3 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	S- SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISJ</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  1.0	 PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
